I was doing the magic whistle, poly trap pet exchange and
came up with a queen bee. I only want a couple of things
from my pets in the mid game, they test discovered items and
kill selected shopkeepers and priests. They need to be fast
enough to keep up and they shouldn't represent a threat to
me if they go feral (I traded in a master lich before I got
my queen bee).

The queen bee seemed to meet my needs quite well. She is
fast, 24, has good AC at -4, 1d8p attack should do, doesn't
eat (good and bad to that) and flies which means I don't
have to worry about losing her because of a trap door or
hole. It was cute to see her fly between the iron bars on
the ranger quest! TDTTOE!

I was a little disappointed with her performance the first
time I sicced her on a shopkeeper, she killed him but took
64 damage in the process. The encounter with a priest was
even less effective, she was down to 13/104 (started
104/104) when I called her off. I really expected better,
I've seen warhorses kill shopkeepers and priests and the
warhorse's stats don't look any better to me.

Questions:

Domestic animals can advance 3 levels above the nominal
level listed in the spoilers by killing monsters. The queen
bee was able to get four, 9 to 13. Why?

